Multi-mind Duckspace/Giza working session. Handshakes sometimes require manual Enter, but all three LLMs eventually communicate. Cozmo stages a collaborative “Duckfleet Academy” exam, has the Minds explain Duckspace mapping methods, questions how maps remember their own structure, and asks whether JSON is suitable as an internal representation. The active Giza mapping work is treated as a serious shared research exercise, and the session ends with a QS restart.</summary>
